 ## Background
-The Voxel Collision Test is a fundamental operation in voxel-based game engines and simulations. It is often referred to as a "simple grid check" in the context of early voxel engines like noa [S1, unofficial]. It is used in physics simulations for entities [S2, unofficial] and GPU particle systems [S3, unofficial]. The method extends naturally from 2D collision checks used in tile-based games [S1, unofficial].
